The second line for every \(N\) gives the initial fidelity \(F_0=|\langle\psi_{\rm target}|0\dots0\rangle|^2\), the starting point of every circuit. It is \(1/2\) for the GHZ state and \(0\) for the W state, and for the non-integrable ground state it falls to almost zero as \(N\) grows, because \(|0\dots0\rangle\) has the highest classical energy of \(\hat{\mathcal H}_{\rm KH}\). The antiferromagnetic coupling favours antiparallel neighbours, and the longitudinal term \(+0.809\sum_i\hat Z_i\) favours spins in \(|1\rangle\). The entanglement entropy of the GHZ state is one bit for every \(N\), and that of the W state equals one bit for even \(N\) and stays slightly below for \(N=3\). The entanglement of the transverse-field ground state at \(h=0.5\) grows towards one bit with \(N\), as the state approaches the GHZ state, and at \(h=2\) it stays near \(0.1\) bit, since the state is close to the product state \(|+\dots+\rangle\). The non-integrable ground state lies in between. The figure collects these values, which we later compare with the difficulty of each target for the agent.


